eflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 17\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Uranium Energy Corp. is a mid-cap energy business with a $3.3B market cap on $37M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -39% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -8% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 31%.","The company is burning through $107M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -64.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 16.1% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 22% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (16.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Energy peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Energy peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 373% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Energy peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 427% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (UEC) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/43/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_UEC_Volatility_110626113802_1794026282.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794026282.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Uranium Energy (UEC) Priced Too Richly On Book Value?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/uranium-energy-uec-priced-too-002024703.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793924424.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.964,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"BC-Most Active Stocks","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/bc-most-active-stocks-153018603.html","date":"20